# deploy/postgres/pg_ident.conf.template
# Rendered verbatim to /etc/postgresql/18/main/pg_ident.conf on the VPS, next to pg_hba.conf.
# PRODUCTION MAPS NO OS USER TO ANY DATABASE ROLE. This file is installed so that no map from
# an earlier copy survives; it must stay without a single active line.
#
# WARNING: the `readiness` map for debateai_staff_readiness_writer (the auth DB batch step) is
# PREVIEW-ONLY. The preview writes it itself, mapping the dedicated no-login OS user
# debateai-readiness (never root), exactly as deploy/preview-lifecycle/v1/README.md step 7 says.
# Do not copy it here: production has no team-unlock helper, and a map from root would let any
# process the kernel reports as uid 0 that reaches the socket log in as that role.
# tests/architecture/vps-deployment-baseline.test.ts fails on any non-comment line.
#
# MAPNAME     SYSTEM-USERNAME   PG-USERNAME
